==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|it}} {{m|la|bonus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈbwɔː.no]|/ˈbwɔno/|lang=it}}
* {{audio|It-buono.ogg|Audio|lang=it}}
* {{hyphenation|buò|no|lang=it}}

===Adjective===
{{it-adj|buon}}

# [[good]]
# [[fair]]

====Usage notes====
* The [[apocopic]] form {{l|it|buon}} and (optionally) the contracted form {{l|it|buon'}} are used before masculine and feminine singular nouns, respectively,  in the same manner as the indefinite article (i.e. ''buon giorno'', ''buon amico'' but ''buono zio'', ''buona sera'' but ''buon'amica'', etc.).

====Synonyms====
* {{l|it|capace}}
* {{l|it|esperto}}
* {{l|it|giusto}}
* {{l|it|onesto}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|it|cattivo}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|it|alla buona}}
* {{l|it|bontà}}
* {{l|it|buonamente}}
* {{l|it|buonanotte}}
* {{l|it|buonasera}}
* {{l|it|buongiorno}}
* {{l|it|buonsenso}}, {{l|it|buon senso}}
* {{l|it|buonumore}}, {{l|it|buon umore}}
* {{l|it|di buon'ora}}

